        "content": "These are plain module-level stores built on `subscribe`/listener sets — the subscribe/emit contract is pure JS and testable **without React** by calling the exported functions directly and asserting the listener fires. Only `useOpenActionId`/`useToolTab`/`useToast` themselves (the `useSyncExternalStore` wrappers) need a component-test harness; the store logic doesn't.\n\n```js\n// tests/stores.test.js\nimport { test } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { openAction, closeAction } from '../features/actions/actionSheetStore.js';\nimport { setToolTab } from '../features/tools/toolTabStore.js';\nimport { showToast, dismissToast } from '../features/feedback/toast.js';\n\n// Note: these modules only export the setter functions and a React hook for\n// reading state — there's no plain getter. To unit test without React, either\n// export a `getSnapshot`-equivalent for tests, or spy via a fake listener.\n\ntest('openAction/closeAction notify subscribers', () => {\n  // TODO: once a non-hook getter exists (or by reaching into module internals via\n  // a test-only export), assert openAction('x') then closeAction() round-trips.\n});\n\ntest('showToast replaces an in-flight toast and auto-dismisses after `duration`', (t) => {\n  t.mock.timers.enable({ apis: ['setTimeout'] });\n  // TODO: showToast('a'); showToast('b') immediately after → only 'b' should be live.\n  // Advance timers past `duration` and assert the toast cleared.\n});\n```\n*(Flagging: these three stores currently offer no way to read `openId`/`active`/`current` outside the React hook. Worth adding a plain `getOpenActionId()`-style export purely so tests don't need a DOM — small, low-risk refactor.)*\n\n",
